WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.189 --> 00:00:04.356
- [Announcer] It's been win,
win, win on Supermarket Sweep.

00:00:05.469 --> 00:00:07.459
- Supermarket Sweep
was an iconic game show

00:00:07.459 --> 00:00:10.037
in the ‘90s and early 2000s.

00:00:10.037 --> 00:00:13.189
- [Announcer] And here is
our host David Ruprecht.

00:00:13.189 --> 00:00:15.022
- Howdy, oh thank you.

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:20.429
But what most people didn't
know: all the meat was fake

00:00:20.429 --> 00:00:23.808
and all the other food had gone bad.

00:00:23.808 --> 00:00:25.376
Are you ready to play the game?

00:00:25.376 --> 00:00:28.048
- [Announcer] Welcome
to Supermarket Sweep.

00:00:28.048 --> 00:00:30.752
(upbeat music)

00:00:30.752 --> 00:00:31.632
- Go Vicky!

00:00:31.632 --> 00:00:34.392
We shot for about five
months, six months every year

00:00:34.392 --> 00:00:38.837
and, uh, they used the same
food over and over again.

00:00:38.837 --> 00:00:41.221
So by about the third month,

00:00:41.221 --> 00:00:44.962
the hot dogs had sort of started
to ferment in the package

00:00:44.962 --> 00:00:46.714
and the package swelled up.

00:00:46.714 --> 00:00:48.394
And, a lot of the food,

00:00:48.394 --> 00:00:51.770
having been thrown in and
out of carts for three,

00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:54.255
four months, had gotten pretty beaten up.

00:00:54.255 --> 00:00:55.492
And one of the things people always ask me

00:00:55.492 --> 00:00:57.270
is: do they get to keep the food?

00:00:57.270 --> 00:01:00.090
And, uh, no, and if they didn't win because

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:02.723
there were three teams,
they got their sweatshirts.

00:01:02.723 --> 00:01:04.935
Unfortunately the winning team did not get

00:01:04.935 --> 00:01:06.793
their sweatshirts, interestingly enough.

00:01:06.793 --> 00:01:09.899
They got $5,000 but they
didn't get their sweatshirts.

00:01:09.899 --> 00:01:12.316
(jazz music)

00:01:15.165 --> 00:01:18.983
I shouldn't be telling you
this, it's a trade secret.

00:01:18.983 --> 00:01:21.600
Very few people know
this and very few people

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:25.642
used this strategy,
but those who did, won.

00:01:25.642 --> 00:01:28.813
Instead of five hams and five turkeys

00:01:28.813 --> 00:01:31.673
that load up your cart, you come over here

00:01:31.673 --> 00:01:35.614
and you get five of these hair
colorings and then you get,

00:01:35.614 --> 00:01:38.579
well we won't mess with maxi pads.

00:01:38.579 --> 00:01:40.666
You get five of all these
expensive health and beauty

00:01:40.666 --> 00:01:44.205
products, with one cart
you can beat everybody.

00:01:44.205 --> 00:01:47.027
Don't tell anybody, it's
just between you and me.

00:01:47.027 --> 00:01:49.521
- I got it, I won, yeah!

00:01:49.521 --> 00:01:51.031
- What a fantasy to be able to run around,

00:01:51.031 --> 00:01:52.671
grab your favorite foods,

00:01:52.671 --> 00:01:54.231
as much of it as you want

00:01:54.231 --> 00:01:56.386
and not have to pay for it.

00:01:56.386 --> 00:01:57.985
This is David Ruprecht saying,

00:01:57.985 --> 00:01:59.533
“Next time you're at the checkout stand

00:01:59.533 --> 00:02:00.807
and you hear the beep,
(beeping)

00:02:00.807 --> 00:02:03.013
think of all the fun you could have on…”

00:02:03.013 --> 00:02:05.027
- [All] Supermarket Sweep.

00:02:05.027 --> 00:02:08.393
(upbeat music)

00:02:08.393 --> 00:02:11.143
(alarms beeping)

